WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.580
A new year is upon us! Are you ready to&nbsp;
make it your best language learning year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.620
ever? I certainly am, thanks to my simple&nbsp;
6-step yearly plan. If you want to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.120
how to crush it in 2023 and take all your&nbsp;
language goals to the next level, stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.640
tuned—because I'm going to show you how right now. Hey, I am Luca Lampariello, I am a language coach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.540
who speaks 14 languages. and on this channel&nbsp;
I help people learn foreign languages more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.820
efficiently, faster and in a fun way.
So, do you want to know how to crush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:35.460
your 2023 language goals? Let’s dive right in!
To make the most of the new year, you need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.180
do two very important things:
Reflect on your progress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:45.180
over the PREVIOUS 365 days
Plan your learning for the NEXT 365 days.&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.320
This is very different from how people&nbsp;
traditionally go about setting their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.940
goals at this point of the year. Typically,&nbsp;
people just set their New Year's Resolutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.840
around what they'd like to accomplish at&nbsp;
the end of the year, and just go for it.&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.000
THIS plan requires a little more thinking,&nbsp;
but it does a better job of setting you up for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.860
success. It encourages you to build upon your&nbsp;
last year of learning experiences by creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.840
an action plan at the three-month, one month,&nbsp;
and daily levels. As a result, you'll always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.460
be aware of what you should be working on,&nbsp;
and you'll always be able to stay on track.&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.760
But enough theory! Let's talk&nbsp;
about the steps of this plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.460
so you can put it into practice and CRUSH 2023! The six steps of the plan are as follows:&nbsp;

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.120
Reflect on your language learning&nbsp;
progress over the past year&nbsp;

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.000
Assess your current language skills
Visualize yourself one year from now&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.480
Establish key goals and objectives&nbsp;
for the next three months&nbsp;

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:46.380
Break down your key goals into daily habits. 
Review (and adjust) your plan every three months&nbsp;

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.100
Step 1: Reflect on your language&nbsp;
learning progress over the past year&nbsp;

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.900
The first thing you must do is look back on&nbsp;
the previous year, and think about all that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.680
you've accomplished in your language learning.
Here, it's useful to ask yourself a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.400
of guiding questions, including:
What went well in the past year?&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.200
What didn't go so well?
In which areas did I improve the most?&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.260
In which areas do I still need to improve?
What were my biggest lessons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.620
learned over the year?
You don't need to be too rigid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.660
with exactly how you go about this. The goal is&nbsp; simply to get a general idea of your recent "wins"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.040
and "losses" so you can use this information to&nbsp;create a more optimized plan for the coming year.&nbsp;

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.500
For example, here's what I wrote when&nbsp;
reflecting on my Hungarian learning for 2022:&nbsp;

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.360
I managed to learn Hungarian very regularly&nbsp;
throughout 2022, spending some time with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.520
language at least 4-5 days each week. Also, I&nbsp;
modified my practice activities to be mainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.020
input-based, as opposed to the output-based&nbsp;
activities I’d been doing previously. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.920
mainly prioritized listening to podcasts&nbsp;
and watching YouTube videos, though I did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.780
read the occasional book, as well. My favorite&nbsp;
podcast resource has been Hungarian with Sziszi.&nbsp;

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.040
2022 was also a great year for my Hungarian&nbsp;
learning because I had the chance to visit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.600
Budapest and spend an entire month there during&nbsp;the summer. I’ve been to Budapest before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.680
but this was the first time that I really felt&nbsp;
comfortable using the language in everyday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.320
life. I also had a much easier time speaking&nbsp;
with natives than I’ve had in previous years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.420
and at one point, I even managed to have a&nbsp;
two-hour conversation with my tutor, Petra!&nbsp;

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:24.060
In terms of takeaways, I can think of three:
Learning (almost) everyday really pays off&nbsp;

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:29.100
Solid input skills are essential in&nbsp;
order to build solid output skills&nbsp;

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.780
Traveling to the country where a language is&nbsp;
spoken can be a great reward for hard work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.260
as well as a worthy challenge&nbsp;that can spur future growth.&nbsp;

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.660
You see? Creating a short-but-sweet synopsis of&nbsp;the previous year's efforts can help you gain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:48.300
a clear perspective on what you have to do next. Speakng of "what you have to do next", let's move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:54.300
on to the second part of our planning process.
Step 2: Assess your current language skills&nbsp;

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.140
When you're learning a language, what you're&nbsp;
actually doing is developing a network of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.340
interconnected skills in your brain. The four&nbsp;
most prominent of these skills are listening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.940
speaking, reading, and writing.
To determine which of the four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:09.840
skills you want to develop in the coming year, you&nbsp;should first take stock of your current abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.680
so you can get a good idea of your&nbsp;
strengths and weaknesses as a learner.&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.580
This is easier than it sounds. All you&nbsp;
have to do for this step is think of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:23.100
few things you're capable of doing in each of&nbsp;
the major skill areas. It may also be useful to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.840
highlight what you currently cannot do in these&nbsp;
areas, so that you know what to work on next.&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.200
Here's how I recently evaluated&nbsp;
my skills for Hungarian:&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.000
Reading
I can read scripts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.960
of podcasts aimed at B2 learners, and I’ve just&nbsp;begun reading books aimed at native speakers.&nbsp;

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.480
Listening
My ability to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:44.820
podcasts and videos has improved drastically. In&nbsp;particular, I’m most comfortable with the podcasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:49.380
that both Sziszi and Petra produce, and I’m even&nbsp;managing to understand YouTube videos on certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:55.260
complex topics. I can’t understand news broadcasts&nbsp;yet, but my listening ability in general is much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.400
improved over where it was one year ago.
Speaking&nbsp;

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.620
I can hold conversations on most everyday topics&nbsp;without major problems. I still hesitate and make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.460
mistakes, of course, but overall I feel quite&nbsp;
comfortable, even during longer conversations.&nbsp;

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.760
Writing. I didn’t focus on building my writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:16.500
skills in 2022, so I can’t really evaluate them&nbsp;
at this point. However, I plan to begin keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.360
a daily journal in Hungarian starting in 2024.
Not too bad, right? The point of this step is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.580
to describe your language abilities in concrete&nbsp;
terms, so that there's less guesswork when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.480
comes to the type of practice you need&nbsp;
to build into your new learning plan.&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:36.420
On to Step 3! Step 3: Visualize yourself one year from now&nbsp;

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.980
The last step was all about objectively&nbsp;
evaluating where your language abilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.080
are. This next step is about emotionally&nbsp;
evaluating where you want your language&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:52.080
abilities to be, one full year from now.
Why bring emotions into a learning plan? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.980
your emotional state strongly influences&nbsp;
how motivated (or unmotivated) you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.300
to do something. If we can tie strong&nbsp;
positive emotions to your language goals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.200
then you'll be much more likely to stick&nbsp;
with them, even when the going gets tough.&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.700
We can build this connection between our emotions&nbsp;and our goals through creating a visualization.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.440
More specifically, by visualizing our future&nbsp;
self after he or she has accomplished all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:31.140
goals that we are about to set in this plan.
I like to treat this as a kind of meditative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:37.680
exercise. I close my eyes, and try to create&nbsp;
a vivid mental picture of myself at the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.100
of the year, doing all the things I want&nbsp;
to be able to do in my target language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.140
Once I've created a sufficiently vivid mental&nbsp;
image, I write it down, so that I can refer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:49.860
it and expand upon it throughout the year.
Here's the end-of-year visualization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.360
I recently created for Hungarian:
31 December, 2023 - I am in Budapest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.740
drinking a glass of pálinka in my friend’s&nbsp;
apartment. We’re having a party, and I’m speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:04.260
Hungarian with the people there. Everyone I talk&nbsp;to is amazed at how well I speak Hungarian. “Wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:08.760
your pronunciation is incredible!” one person&nbsp;
says. “You’re so fluent!” says another. I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.780
excited, because I plan on spending several&nbsp;
months in Budapest in 2024, and I’ll surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:18.300
improve even more by then. The future is bright!
This kind of visualization exercise may sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:22.020
corny at first, but I can assure you&nbsp;
that the results can be quite powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:27.660
especially when you keep the written version handy&nbsp;and look at it whenever you're tired, stressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:32.100
or otherwise unmotivated to learn.
Ok, time for Step 4!&nbsp;

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:36.360
Step 4: Establish key goals and&nbsp;
objectives for the next three months&nbsp;

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:41.460
The previous steps should have given you a good&nbsp;idea of where you need and want to improve your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:45.720
language skills by the end of the year.
It's time now to take those general ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:52.200
and boil them down to concrete goals—to things you&nbsp;absolutely want to accomplish in the next 90 days.&nbsp;

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.300
Why 90 days? Because that's how we're&nbsp;
going to take the whole year and make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:03.000
it a bit more digestible. Instead of thinking&nbsp;
about all 365 days at once, we'll primarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.680
focus on 90 days at a time, which helps us&nbsp;
remain focused in the short and medium-term.&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.820
So, ask yourself: based upon your previous&nbsp;
year's learning, your current level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:16.920
and your visualization, what do you want to have&nbsp;accomplished by the end of the next three months?&nbsp;

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:20.700
Your answer can be anything, so long as it&nbsp;
leads you towards the version of yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:25.980
you just pictured in your visualization.
Here are the language goals that I want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:31.500
to accomplish by the end of March 2023:
I want to able to understand most podcasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:36.180
aimed at learners, especially Sziszi’s&nbsp;
podcasts, even the most difficult ones.&nbsp;

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:43.140
I want to be able to understand YouTube&nbsp;
videos to a good 60-70 % without subtitles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:47.580
be it content for Hungarian learners&nbsp;
or for native Hungarian speakers.&nbsp;

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:53.700
I want to be able to understand at least a&nbsp;
good 60-70% of the news without subtitles.&nbsp;

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:57.540
I want to be able to greatly improve my&nbsp;
reading skills, especially when it comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:03.420
to reading books, be it non-fiction or novels.
I want to improve my spoken fluency to a level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:08.520
where I feel comfortable speaking both with my&nbsp;teacher and native Hungarian speakers in general.&nbsp;

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.480
Step 5: Break down your&nbsp;
key goals into daily habits&nbsp;

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:18.120
Goals are useful for providing a “finish line”,&nbsp;
but do little to help you manage the day-to-day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.100
work of language learning. You've just created&nbsp;
your three-month goals, but the key now is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:27.720
to take those goals and identify the daily&nbsp;
actions that will help you reach them. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:32.700
daily actions will constitute your “habits”.
Any habit will suffice here, so long as it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:37.680
consists of something that, if done daily, will&nbsp;
realistically get you to your three-month goal.&nbsp;

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:42.540
In the last section, I mentioned that I want to&nbsp;be able to listen to a certain level of podcast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.080
watch a certain level of YouTube video&nbsp;
without difficulty, and even watch the news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.880
comfortably. To do that, I'll naturally have&nbsp;
to spend daily time consuming more podcasts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:56.100
videos and news until I reach that level.
Here is a list of a few habits that come directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.100 --> 00:10:02.400
from the goals I have established for 2023:
I want to listen to at least one episode of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.600
the Hungarian with Sziszi podcast every day,&nbsp;
and even take her course, once it’s available!&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.780
I want to watch at least 3 YouTube videos a week. I want to watch the Hungarian news for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:16.620
at least five minutes a day.
I want to be read at the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:21.000
least 2-3 pages of a book every week.
I want to talk to my Hungarian tutor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.240
Petra at least once a week and&nbsp;
review the lesson 24 hours later&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.900
Step 6: Review (and adjust)&nbsp;
your plan every three months&nbsp;

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:33.180
The last step in our six-step planning sequence&nbsp;is actually a recurring one. Every three months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:36.060
you should take out your learning&nbsp;
plan to review and revise it&nbsp;

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:41.760
Additionally, you should revisit Steps 4 and&nbsp;
5, and come up with both goals and habits for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:47.040
the next three months. Naturally, since the year&nbsp;
can be divided up into four periods of 90 days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:53.520
you'll have to come up with four 90-day plans&nbsp;
before the year is done, so keep that in mind.&nbsp;

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.600
Since it's only January, and this is something&nbsp;
you'll have to do regularly throughout the year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.680
I recommend using a calendar or setting up&nbsp;
some kind of recurring reminder for you to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:06.180
return to your plan every three months&nbsp;
and set up your new goals and habits.&nbsp;

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.800
Alright, those are all the steps of my&nbsp;
six-part annual language learning plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.980
Sitting down every January to plan&nbsp;
my language learning like this has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.820
done wonders for my ability to stay focused&nbsp;
and make serious progress in recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.420
so I'm certain that it will create&nbsp;
powerful results for you, as well.&nbsp;

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:25.200
Let's quickly recap the six&nbsp;
steps of the planning process:&nbsp;

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:28.320
Reflect on your language learning&nbsp;
progress over the past year&nbsp;

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:33.540
Assess your current language skills
Visualize yourself one year from now&nbsp;

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.080
Establish key goals and objectives&nbsp;
for the next three months&nbsp;

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:44.160
Break down your key goals into daily habits
Review (and adjust) your plan every three months

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.840
Before we go, I want to leave you with one&nbsp;
final tip: once you write out your yearly plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:52.980
print it out, decorate it, and leave it&nbsp;
somewhere where you'll always see it when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:57.120
you sit down to learn. This will serve as&nbsp;
a powerful reminder of why you're learning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.320
and also help you remember to review&nbsp;
and revise the plan as the year goes on.&nbsp;

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.920
If you'd like to learn more about&nbsp;
how I plan my language learning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.940
check the links in the description box,&nbsp;
as I've left some goodies for you there.&nbsp;

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:13.380
In any case, thanks for watching. I wish&nbsp;
you all the best as you begin this new year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:17.400
and I sincerely hope you're able to achieve&nbsp;
all of your language goals by year's end.&nbsp;

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:21.300
See you next time! Until&nbsp;
then, happy language learning!

